{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790361402,"nonce":"EKmqthsEBrWWskx5cUzixSilvyw=","title":"Async results of 0 read as Pending, and negative results as failure","message":"A poll function is `extern \"C\" fn(*mut u8) -\u003e i64`, shaped by `reshape_to_poll_abi` (crates/passes/krio_adapter/src/abi_emit.rs): it returns 0 for Pending and the result cast to i64 for Ready, with a void return encoded as 1. A result whose i64 is 0 (`0`, `false`, a null pointer, the bits of `0.0`) cannot be told from Pending: `ZyntaxPromise::poll`, `drive_until`, `host_futures::resolve_future`, the awaiting parent's poll block and `generate_sync_entry`'s loop all keep polling. `ZyntaxPromise::poll` also reports every negative result as `Failed(\"Async operation failed with code N\")`. The same ABI serves the sync entry of a function performing a resumable effect, so such a function whose result is 0 loops in its entry. The loops follow from the code and have not been reproduced.\n\nDone: status and value travel separately (a status return, with the value in an outcome slot of the state machine), every reader of a poll result uses the status, and async functions and resumable-effect performers returning 0, false and negative values complete with those values. e9086df7a988adbd490fd072b65be7ffa70295a5b4aaecc653b39fd078d4ce51 asks for the same ABI change for Python.","files":null}]}